<div class="entry-content single-content">
	
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">How much wallpaper do you need? This free <strong>wallpaper calculator</strong> works it out drop by drop: it counts the drops (strips) your wall needs, how many drops you get from each roll once you allow for trimming and the pattern repeat, and turns that into the number of rolls to buy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Choose a feature wall or a whole room, type the size and pick the pattern. It works in meters or feet, and you can change the roll size under <em>More options</em> if your wallpaper is not a standard 52 to 53 cm (20.5 to 21 in) wide roll.</p>



<div id="dsh-wp" class="dsh-calc">

<h3>How many rolls of wallpaper do you need?</h3>
<p class="sub">Choose a feature wall or a whole room, type the size and pick the pattern. The rolls appear right away.</p>
<div class="row"><div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Units"><button type="button" data-u="m">meters</button><button type="button" data-u="ft">feet</button></div></div>
<fieldset><legend>1. What are you papering?</legend>
<div class="opts" role="group" aria-label="Area">
<button type="button" data-a="wall" class="on"><b>One wall</b><span>A feature wall</span></button>
<button type="button" data-a="room"><b>Whole room</b><span>All four walls</span></button>
</div>
<div class="grid">
<label id="lw"><span id="tw">Wall width</span> <span data-lu="l"></span><input type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" step="0.01" id="ww"></label>
<label id="lr" class="hide"><span>Room width</span> <span data-lu="l"></span><input type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" step="0.01" id="rw"></label>
